The Count in Python after Scott Adams, 1979

the main program is main.py
in 'requirements.txt' are the requirements for the program

on 10-09-2026:

altgraph==0.17.5
packaging==26.3
pefile==2024.8.26
pillow==12.3.0
pyinstaller==6.22.2
pyinstaller-hooks-contrib==2026.7
pywin32-ctypes==0.2.3

start the program:
py main.py [--delay 200]

the delay is im ms, to see it scroll at a given rate in auto mode.
At 200 ms the program takes about 35 s to play "auto 10"  (165 moves)
at 50 ms the program takes 10 s to play the same "auto"
at 5000 ms the program takes about 18 minutes to play, nearly the
same as ./documents/The Count walkthrough.mp4

The walkthrough in the subfolder 'auto', it can be edited with Notepad
or any development tool.
When you enter 'auto 10' the file ./auto/script_10.txt will be used.

This is not a complete implementation of the original game of 1979,
but it completes the job.

most important verbs:
LOO       looks around the current room
GET ...   pick up an item ... in the current room
DRO ...   drop item ... in the current room
INV       player's inventory
GO  ...   go in a given direction
ENT ...   enter a room/window to go to another room
HEL       the help is only implemented in two or three rooms
AUT ...   execute as script 1 .. 10 in folder auto

nice to haves that are NOT implemented:
SAV  ...  save the current state
LOA  ...  reload the current state
REC  ...  record input

most important 'nouns':
SHE       sheet
STA       tent stake
MAL       rubber mallet
COF       coffin

backdoor/debug command:
WHE       where are the game objects?